n of Pharaoh (Gen. 45:17-25), Jacob and his sons went down into Egypt.","verses":774,"father":"Amram","mother":"Jochebed","v":[1,3,16,17,26,30]},{"id":"israel_682","name":"Israel","also":"","summary":"One who follows on another’s heels; supplanter, (Gen. 25:26; 27:36; Hos. 12:2-4), the second born of the twin sons of Isaac by Rebekah. He was born probably at Lahai-roi, when his father was fifty-nine and Abraham one hundred and fifty-nine years old.","verses":1009,"father":"Isaac","mother":"Rebekah","v":[2,3,24,26,32]},{"id":"canaan_914","name":"Canaan","also":"Canaanites, Canaanite","summary":"The fourth son of Ham (Gen. 10:6). His descendants were under a curse in consequence of the transgression of his father (9:22-27). His eldest son, Zidon, was the father of the Sidonians and Phoenicians.","verses":84,"father":"Ham","mother":"","v":[2,17]},{"id":"reuben_2429","name":"Reuben","also":"","summary":"Behold a son!, the eldest son of Jacob and Leah (Gen. 29:32). His sinful conduct, referred to in Gen. 35:22, brought down upon him his dying father’s malediction (48:4).","verses":70,"father":"Israel","mother":"Leah","v":[4]},{"id":"shammua_2545","name":"Shammua","also":"","summary":"One of the spies sent out by Moses to search the land (Num. 13:4).","verses":1,"father":"Zaccur","mother":"","v":[4]},{"id":"zaccur_2963","name":"Zaccur","also":"","summary":"Father of Shammua, who was one of the spies sent out by Moses (Num. 13:4).","verses":1,"father":"","mother":"","v":[4]},{"id":"simeon_2741","name":"Simeon","also":"","summary":"The second son of Jacob by Leah (Gen. 29:33). He was associated with Levi in the terrible act of vengeance against Hamor and the Shechemites (34:25, 26).","verses":40,"father":"Israel","mother":"Leah","v":[5]},{"id":"hori_1553","name":"Hori","also":"","summary":"","verses":1,"father":"","mother":"","v":[5]},{"id":"shaphat_2552","name":"Shaphat","also":"","summary":"One of the spies.","verses":1,"father":"Hori","mother":"","v":[5]},{"id":"judah_1751","name":"Judah","also":"","summary":"Praise, the fourth son of Jacob by Leah.","verses":245,"father":"Israel","mother":"Leah","v":[6]},{"id":"caleb_537","name":"Caleb","also":"","summary":"The son of Jephunneh (Num. 13:6; 32:12; Josh. 14:6, 14). He was one of those whom Moses sent to search the land in the second year after the Exodus.","verses":30,"father":"Jephunneh","mother":"","v":[6,30]},{"id":"jephunneh_840","name":"Jephunneh","also":"","summary":"The father of Caleb, who was Joshua’s companion in exploring Canaan (Num. 13:6), a Kenezite (Josh. 14:14).","verses":15,"father":"","mother":"","v":[6]},{"id":"issachar_645","name":"Issachar","also":"","summary":"Hired (Gen. 30:18). “God hath given me,” said Leah, “my hire (Heb. sekhari)...and she called his name Issachar.” He was Jacob’s ninth son, and was born in Padan-aram (comp. 28:2).","verses":38,"father":"Israel","mother":"Leah","v":[7]},{"id":"igal_1598","name":"Igal","also":"","summary":"Num. 13:7, one of the spies of the tribe of Issachar.","verses":1,"father":"Joseph","mother":"","v":[7]},{"id":"joseph_1711","name":"Joseph","also":"","summary":"Father of Issachar Igal.","verses":1,"father":"","mother":"","v":[7]},{"id":"joshua_1727","name":"Joshua","also":"Jehoshua, Oshea, Jesus, Jeshua, Hoshea","summary":"Jehovah is his help, or Jehovah the Saviour. The son of Nun, of the tribe of Ephraim, the successor of Moses as the leader of Israel.","verses":189,"father":"Nun","mother":"","v":[8,16]},{"id":"ephraim_1206","name":"Ephraim","also":"","summary":"Double fruitfulness (“for God had made him fruitful in the land of his affliction”). The second son of Joseph, born in Egypt (Gen. 41:52; 46:20).","verses":160,"father":"Joseph","mother":"Asenath","v":[8]},{"id":"nun_2214","name":"Nun","also":"Non","summary":"Beyond the fact that he was the father of Joshua nothing more is known of him (Ex. 33:11).","verses":30,"father":"Elishama","mother":"","v":[8,16]},{"id":"benjamin_463","name":"Benjamin","also":"Ben-oni","summary":"The younger son of Jacob by Rachel (Gen. 35:18). His birth took place at Ephrath, on the road between Bethel and Bethlehem, at a short distance from the latter place.","verses":157,"father":"Israel","mother":"Rachel","v":[9]},{"id":"palti_2269","name":"Palti","also":"","summary":"Deliverance from the Lord, one of the spies representing the tribe of Benjamin (Num. 13:9).","verses":1,"father":"Raphu","mother":"","v":[9]},{"id":"raphu_2397","name":"Raphu","also":"","summary":"Healed, a Benjamite, whose son Palti was one of the twelve spies (Num. 13:9).","verses":1,"father":"","mother":"","v":[9]},{"id":"zebulun_3002","name":"Zebulun","also":"Zabulon","summary":"Dwelling, the sixth and youngest son of Jacob and Leah (Gen. 30:20). Little is known of his personal history.","verses":46,"father":"Israel","mother":"Leah","v":[10]},{"id":"gaddiel_1265","name":"Gaddiel","also":"","summary":"Fortune (i.e., sent) of God, the representative of the tribe of Zebulum among the twelve spies (Num. 13:10).","verses":1,"father":"Sodi","mother":"","v":[10]},{"id":"sodi_2761","name":"Sodi","also":"","summary":"","verses":1,"father":"","mother":"","v":[10]},{"id":"joseph_1710","name":"Joseph","also":"Zaphnath-paaneah","summary":"The elder of the two sons of Jacob by Rachel (Gen. 30:23, 24), who, on the occasion of his birth, said, “God hath taken away [Heb. ‘asaph] my reproach.”","verses":199,"father":"Israel","mother":"Rachel","v":[11]},{"id":"manasseh_1928","name":"Manasseh","also":"Manasses","summary":"The elder of the two sons of Joseph. He and his brother Ephraim were afterwards adopted by Jacob as his own sons (48:1).","verses":109,"father":"Joseph","mother":"Asenath","v":[11]},{"id":"gaddi_1264","name":"Gaddi","also":"","summary":"Fortunate, the representative of the tribe of Manasseh among the twelve “spies” sent by Moses to spy the land (Num. 13:11).","verses":1,"father":"Susi","mother":"","v":[11]},{"id":"susi_2805","name":"Susi","also":"","summary":"The father of Gaddi, who was one of the twelve spies (Num. 13:11).","verses":1,"father":"","mother":"","v":[11]},{"id":"dan_973","name":"Dan","also":"","summary":"The fifth son of Jacob. His mother was Bilhah, Rachel’s maid (Gen. 30:6, “God hath judged me”, Heb. dananni).","verses":63,"father":"Israel","mother":"Bilhah","v":[12]},{"id":"ammiel_220","name":"Ammiel","also":"","summary":"One of the twelve spies sent by Moses to search the land of Canaan (Num. 13:12).","verses":1,"father":"Gemalli","mother":"","v":[12]},{"id":"gemalli_1294","name":"Gemalli","also":"","summary":"","verses":1,"father":"","mother":"","v":[12]},{"id":"asher_337","name":"Asher","also":"Aser","summary":"Happy, Jacob’s eigth son; his mother was Zilpah, Leah’s handmaid (Gen. 30:13). Of the tribe founded by him nothing is recorded beyond its holding a place in the list of the tribes (35:26; 46:17; Ex. 1:4, etc.) It increased in numbers twenty-nine percent, during the thirty-eight years’ wanderings.","verses":43,"father":"Israel","mother":"Zilpah","v":[13]},{"id":"michael_2058","name":"Michael","also":"","summary":"The father of Sethur, the spy selected to represent Asher (Num. 13:13).","verses":1,"father":"","mother":"","v":[13]},{"id":"sethur_2505","name":"Sethur","also":"","summary":"Hidden, one of the spies sent to search the Promised Land.","verses":1,"father":"Michael","mother":"","v":[13]},{"id":"naphtali_2149","name":"Naphtali","also":"Nephthalim","summary":"My wrestling, the fifth son of Jacob. His mother was Bilhah, Rachel’s handmaid (Gen. 30:8). When Jacob went down into Egypt, Naphtali had four sons (Gen. 46:24).","verses":49,"father":"Israel","mother":"Bilhah","v":[14]},{"id":"nahbi_2141","name":"Nahbi","also":"","summary":"Hidden, one of the twelve spies sent out to explore the land of Canaan (Num. 13:14).","verses":1,"father":"Vophsi","mother":"","v":[14]},{"id":"vophsi_2938","name":"Vophsi","also":"","summary":"","verses":1,"father":"","mother":"","v":[14]},{"id":"gad_1262","name":"Gad","also":"","summary":"Jacob’s seventh son, by Zilpah, Leah’s handmaid, and the brother of Asher (Gen. 30:11-13; 46:16, 18).","verses":55,"father":"Israel","mother":"Zilpah","v":[15]},{"id":"geuel_1309","name":"Geuel","also":"","summary":"","verses":1,"father":"Machi","mother":"","v":[15]},{"id":"machi_1876","name":"Machi","also":"","summary":"","verses":1,"father":"","mother":"","v":[15]},{"id":"anak_252","name":"Anak","also":"Anakims","summary":"Long-necked, the son of Arba, father of the Anakim (Josh. 15:13; 21:11, Heb. Anok).","verses":8,"father":"Arba","mother":"","v":[22,28,33]},{"id":"ahiman_146","name":"Ahiman","also":"","summary":"One of the three giant Anakim brothers whom Caleb and the spies saw in Mount Hebron (Num. 13:22) when they went in to explore the land.","verses":3,"father":"Anak","mother":"","v":[22]},{"id":"sheshai_2671","name":"Sheshai","also":"","summary":"","verses":3,"father":"Anak","mother":"","v":[22]},{"id":"talmai_2818","name":"Talmai","also":"","summary":"One of the Anakim of Hebron, who were slain by the men of Judah under Caleb (Num. 13:22; Josh. 15:14; Judg. 1:10).","verses":3,"father":"Anak","mother":"","v":[22]},{"id":"aaron_1","name":"Aaron","also":"","summary":"The eldest son of Amram and Jochebed, a daughter of Levi (Ex. 6:20). Some explain the name as meaning mountaineer, others mountain of strength, illuminator.","verses":331,"father":"Amram","mother":"Jochebed","v":[26]}],"places":[{"id":"canaan_272","name":"Canaan","kind":"Region (Country)","lat":31.69353,"lon":34.84388,"summary":"The country which derived its name from the preceding. The name as first used by the Phoenicians denoted only the maritime plain on which Sidon was built.","verses":76,"v":[2,17]},{"id":"paran_921","name":"Paran","kind":"Settlement","lat":28.71752,"lon":33.60963,"summary":"Abounding in foliage, or abounding in caverns, (Gen. 21:21), a desert tract forming the north-eastern division of the peninsula of Sinai, lying between the ‘Arabah on the east and the wilderness of Shur on the west.","verses":8,"v":[3,26]},{"id":"negeb_885","name":"Negeb","kind":"Region","lat":30.25,"lon":34.75,"summary":"Heb. Negeb, that arid district to the south of Palestine through which lay the caravan route from Central Palestine to Egypt (Gen. 12:9; 13:1, 3; 46:1-6).","verses":36,"v":[17,22,29]},{"id":"lebo-hamath_723","name":"Lebo-hamath","kind":"","lat":34.19744,"lon":36.34204,"summary":"","verses":10,"v":[21]},{"id":"rehob_987","name":"Rehob","kind":"","lat":33.21935,"lon":35.54412,"summary":"The same, probably, as Beth-rehob (2 Sam. 10:6, 8; Judg. 18:28), a place in the north of Palestine (Num. 13:21).","verses":2,"v":[21]},{"id":"zin_1261","name":"Zin","kind":"Region","lat":30.68771,"lon":34.4948,"summary":"A low palm-tree, the south-eastern corner of the desert et-Tih, the wilderness of Paran, between the Gulf of Akabah and the head of the Wady Guraiyeh (Num. 13:21).","verses":7,"v":[21]},{"id":"egypt_362","name":"Egypt","kind":"Region (Country)","lat":26.4902,"lon":29.8808,"summary":"The land of the Nile and the pyramids, the oldest kingdom of which we have any record, holds a place of great significance in Scripture.","verses":564,"v":[22]},{"id":"hebron_551","name":"Hebron","kind":"City","lat":31.52435,"lon":35.10854,"summary":"A city in the south end of the valley of Eshcol, about midway between Jerusalem and Beersheba, from which it is distant about 20 miles in a straight line.","verses":56,"v":[22]},{"id":"zoan_1270","name":"Zoan","kind":"City","lat":30.97462,"lon":31.88417,"summary":"(Old Egypt. Sant= “stronghold,” the modern San). A city on the Tanitic branch of the Nile, called by the Greeks Tanis.","verses":7,"v":[22]},{"id":"brook_eshcol_1202","name":"brook Eshcol","kind":"Valley","lat":31.5491,"lon":35.09356,"summary":"A valley in which the spies obtained a fine cluster of grapes (Num. 13:23, 24; “the brook Eshcol,” A.V.; “the valley of Eshcol,” R.V.), which they took back with them to the camp of Israel as a specimen of the fruits of the Promised Land.","verses":4,"v":[23,24]},{"id":"kadesh_661","name":"Kadesh","kind":"Oasis","lat":30.64805,"lon":34.42261,"summary":"Holy, or Kadesh-Barnea, sacred desert of wandering, a place on the south-eastern border of Palestine, about 165 miles from Horeb. It lay in the “wilderness” or “desert of Zin” (Gen. 14:7; Num. 13:3-26; 14:29-33; 20:1; 27:14), on the border of Edom (20:16).","verses":15,"v":[26]},{"id":"jordan_653","name":"Jordan","kind":"Water (River)","lat":33.18645,"lon":35.61916,"summary":"But besides these two historical fountains there is a third, called the Hasbany, which rises in the bottom of a valley at the western base of Hermon, 12 miles north of Tell-el-Kady.","verses":177,"v":[29]}],"events":[{"id":"birth_of_caleb_123","title":"Birth of Caleb","year":-1529,"summary":"Passage: Numbers 13:6. People: Caleb.","v":[6]}],"traditions":[],"sources":["JFB","MHCC","Wesley"],"tags":{"bsb":[[3068,3068,3068,1696,413,4872],[7971,7971,0,0,582,8446,8446,8446,776,776,3667,3667,834,589,5414,5414,1121,1121,1121,3605,3605,1,1,1,4294,7971,259,376,5387,5387,5387,5387,0,0],[5921,5921,6310,6310,3068,3068,3068,4872,7971,7971,853,4057,4057,4057,6290,6290,3605,582,582,7218,7218,3478,3478,3478],[428,428,8034,8034,8034,4294,4294,4294,7205,7205,8051,1121,2139,2139],[4294,4294,4294,8095,8095,8202,1121,2753,2753],[4294,4294,4294,3063,3063,3612,1121,3312,3312],[4294,4294,4294,3485,3485,3008,1121,3130,3130],[4294,4294,4294,669,669,1954,1121,5126,5126],[4294,4294,4294,1144,1144,6406,1121,7505,7505],[4294,4294,4294,2074,2074,1427,1121,5476,5476],[4294,4294,4294,4519,4519,4294,4294,3130,3130,1426,1121,5485,5485],[4294,4294,4294,1835,1835,5988,1121,1582,1582],[4294,4294,4294,836,836,5639,1121,4317,4317],[4294,4294,4294,5321,5321,5147,1121,2058,2058],[4294,4294,4294,4294,1410,1410,1345,1121,4352,4352],[428,8034,8034,8034,582,582,582,4872,7971,8446,8446,8446,776,776,4872,4872,7121,1954,1954,1121,5126,5126,3091,3091,3091],[4872,4872,7971,853,8446,8446,8446,776,776,3667,